  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{12}-(-\\frac{25}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
